  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the app to explain how to delete my HFR account and to wipe this app's data, so that I exercise my rights as App Store 5.1.1(v) expects.\n\n### Scope\n\nIn-app screen (decided by the operator 2026-10-27) explaining that the account belongs to HFR and linking **HFR's own account procedure** (opened in the browser); no mail, no hard-coded address (Q-10). Plus 'remove all data from this device' (accounts, cookies, drafts, caches). The HFR page or URL describing the procedure is a forum fact: taken from CAP-N6 (#174), never guessed.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP (App Store release blocker)\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'account deletion mail (Q-10)'; FEATURES 'Not to lose': account deletion (App Store 5.1.1(v))\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `PlusTab.swift` (`AccountDeletionView`; its `DeleteAccountMailComposeView` mail flow is **not** carried over, operator 2026-10-27)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-157-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-081 (#99, in-progress)\n- LOT-119 (#210)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ncapture CAP-N6 (#174): HFR's own account-deletion procedure (the page or URL is a forum fact, never guessed; see Scope and \"Captures needed\"); dependencies LOT-081 (#99) and LOT-119 (#210) are done\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N6 (#174): HFR's own account-deletion procedure: the forum page or URL that explains it (charter, FAQ, profile settings or contact page)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The linked URL comes from CAP-N6 (#174) and is recorded in HFR-PROTOCOL; no mail composer and no e-mail address in source (Q-10).\n- [ ] Wipe leaves no Keychain item, cookie or draft (test).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
